WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.836 --> 00:00:03.112
Hello and welcome to The English

00:00:03.112 --> 00:00:05.468
We Speak with me, Feifei ...

00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:09.019
... and me, Roy. Feifei, did you get me

00:00:09.019 --> 00:00:10.568
a drink of water?

00:00:10.568 --> 00:00:15.549
No, I did not! Go and get yourself one!

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:17.146
But I thought you were bringing me one

00:00:17.146 --> 00:00:18.132
because I overheard you

00:00:18.132 --> 00:00:19.204
saying to Neil that I was

00:00:19.204 --> 00:00:20.461
really thirsty.

00:00:20.461 --> 00:00:23.721
Oh right. Sorry. You weren't meant to hear

00:00:23.721 --> 00:00:27.059
that. I meant that you're thirsty on social

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:29.657
media. You're always posting photos

00:00:29.657 --> 00:00:31.549
of yourself trying to get

00:00:31.549 --> 00:00:33.517
compliments and attention.

00:00:33.517 --> 00:00:37.210
I most certainly am not. What makes

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.548
you think that I post on

00:00:38.548 --> 00:00:41.562
social media just to get attention?

00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:44.146
I have seen some of your elaborate

00:00:44.146 --> 00:00:46.698
and ridiculous photos! You posted

00:00:46.698 --> 00:00:48.400
one the other day with

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.746
a big rat and another where you

00:00:50.746 --> 00:00:53.840
were dressed as a superhero!

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.653
I didn't do that to get attention - I'm not

00:00:57.653 --> 00:01:01.147
thirsty! And it wasn't a big rat, it was my

00:01:01.156 --> 00:01:02.773
dog!

00:01:02.773 --> 00:01:06.737
Right, let's listen to some examples.

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:12.007
Geoff said Sandra's photos were attention-

00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:14.802
seeking. I told him she's thirsty.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.374
Stop being so thirsty. Why do you always

00:01:19.374 --> 00:01:21.949
have to post photos just to get attention?

00:01:23.207 --> 00:01:25.782
Vladimir is so thirsty. He's always

00:01:25.782 --> 00:01:27.439
sharing photos of himself

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:30.055
and a puppy - just to get likes!

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.259
This is The English We Speak from BBC

00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:37.167
Learning English and we're

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.587
talking about the word 'thirsty',

00:01:39.587 --> 00:01:41.982
which is an adjective to describe

00:01:41.982 --> 00:01:44.276
people who are trying very hard

00:01:44.276 --> 00:01:45.756
to get attention and

00:01:45.756 --> 00:01:47.234
praise.

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:49.993
I must admit - a lot of people on social

00:01:49.993 --> 00:01:51.823
media seem really thirsty.

00:01:51.823 --> 00:01:53.371
They're always posting

00:01:53.371 --> 00:01:56.562
photos to get likes. You can also say that

00:01:56.562 --> 00:01:59.372
someone is 'fishing for compliments'.

00:01:59.372 --> 00:02:02.616
Or 'attention-seeking'. That's another way

00:02:02.616 --> 00:02:06.389
of saying 'thirsty'. Which reminds me - you

00:02:06.389 --> 00:02:09.097
look really hot. Do you still want

00:02:09.097 --> 00:02:10.690
that drink of water?

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:14.355
Yes, please! I'm really thirsty.

00:02:14.355 --> 00:02:17.669
Haha got you! I recorded you

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:20.444
admitting that you're really thirsty.

00:02:20.457 --> 00:02:22.160
Next time you post

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.997
something, I have proof.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.391
But I only wanted a drink.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.780
Get it yourself! Bye Roy!

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.760
Oh Bye!

